# Migrate Database from PostgreSQL to MongoDB

1. Analyze current workload and data models to determine if a full migration is feasible.
2. Evaluate existing database schema and identify document-heavy collections or entities that will require conversion.
3. Design a strategy for migrating documents, including any necessary changes in querying patterns and data structures.
4. Implement the migration process, ensuring backward compatibility and data integrity during transition.
5. Test the new MongoDB setup to ensure smooth operation with the updated schema and data models.
